      "id": "18voreu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. WHY SENTENCE STRUCTURE IS A HIGH-SCORING TOPIC"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sentences are constructed using three main building blocks and can be categorized into four types based on structure.",
        "Simple sentences are defined by structure rather than length, compound sentences join two equal ideas, and complex sentences pair one main clause with one dependent clause.",
        "Top structure errors in competitive exams include parallel structure violations, misplaced modifiers, and dangling modifiers.",
        "Sentence transformations require proficiency in swapping active/passive voice, assertive/interrogative/exclamatory/imperative forms, and degree adjustments.",
        "Key conversion patterns involve structural paired connectors like 'TOO…TO / SO…THAT' and 'NOT ONLY…BUT ALSO'."
      ],
      "id": "hkhkwrl"
    },
